@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+## Why
+
+Services need to change stored and exchanged JSON documents with the standard patch format (RFC 6902) instead of ad-hoc update code.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `applyPatch(document, patch)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, implementing RFC 6902 with the operations `add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy` and `test`.
+- The result is a new value; the input document and patch are never mutated.
+- An invalid patch or a failing operation throws an error (no partial result is returned).
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `json-patch`: applying an RFC 6902 JSON Patch to a JSON document.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/index.ts` (new export, reuses the existing JSON Pointer parsing), `src/index.test.ts`.
+- No new dependencies.
