+## ADDED Requirements
+
+### Requirement: Apply a patch without mutation
+`applyPatch(document, patch)` SHALL apply the operations of `patch`, an array, in order, each to the result of the previous one, and return the resulting document. The input `document` and `patch` SHALL NOT be mutated, and the result SHALL NOT share mutable structure with the input. If any operation fails, it SHALL throw an error.
+
+#### Scenario: Input untouched
+- **WHEN** a patch is applied to `{"a": {"b": 1}}` with `{"op":"replace","path":"/a/b","value":2}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"a":{"b":2}}` and the original document still has `b` equal to `1`
+
+#### Scenario: Empty patch
+- **WHEN** the patch is `[]`
+- **THEN** the document is returned unchanged in value
+
+#### Scenario: Operation failure
+- **WHEN** an operation fails after earlier operations succeeded
+- **THEN** an error is thrown and no result is returned
+
+### Requirement: Validate the patch
+`applyPatch` SHALL throw if the patch is not an array, if an operation is not an object, if `op` is not one of the six operation names, if `path` is missing or not a valid JSON Pointer, if `value` is missing for `add`, `replace` or `test`, or if `from` is missing or not a valid JSON Pointer for `move` and `copy`.
+
+#### Scenario: Unknown operation
+- **WHEN** an operation has `"op": "increment"`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Missing value
+- **WHEN** an `add` operation has no `value` member
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Null value is a value
+- **WHEN** an `add` operation has `"value": null`
+- **THEN** it is accepted and null is added
+
+### Requirement: add operation
+`add` SHALL set the value at `path`. With the empty path it SHALL replace the whole document. On an object it SHALL add the member, or replace it if it exists. On an array, the last token SHALL be an index from 0 to the array length, inserting before that position and shifting later elements, or `-`, appending. The parent of the target MUST exist; otherwise an error SHALL be thrown.
+
+#### Scenario: Insert into array
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"add","path":"/a/1","value":"x"}` is applied to `{"a":["p","q"]}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"a":["p","x","q"]}`
+
+#### Scenario: Append with dash
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"add","path":"/a/-","value":"x"}` is applied to `{"a":["p"]}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"a":["p","x"]}`
+
+#### Scenario: Index beyond length or missing parent
+- **WHEN** the index is greater than the array length, or the parent does not exist
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+### Requirement: remove operation
+`remove` SHALL delete the value at `path`, which MUST exist, otherwise an error SHALL be thrown. Removing an array element SHALL shift later elements down. The `-` token SHALL NOT refer to an existing element.
+
+#### Scenario: Remove array element
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"remove","path":"/a/0"}` is applied to `{"a":[1,2]}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"a":[2]}`
+
+#### Scenario: Remove missing target
+- **WHEN** the path does not exist
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+### Requirement: replace operation
+`replace` SHALL set the value at `path`, which MUST exist, otherwise an error SHALL be thrown. With the empty path it SHALL replace the whole document.
+
+#### Scenario: Replace member
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"replace","path":"/a","value":1}` is applied to `{"a":2}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"a":1}`
+
+#### Scenario: Replace missing target
+- **WHEN** the path does not exist
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+### Requirement: move operation
+`move` SHALL remove the value at `from`, which MUST exist, and add it at `path` as `add` would. A `from` that is a proper prefix of `path` SHALL cause an error. Moving a location onto itself SHALL leave the document unchanged.
+
+#### Scenario: Move member
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"move","from":"/a","path":"/b"}` is applied to `{"a":1}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"b":1}`
+
+#### Scenario: Move into own child
+- **WHEN** `from` is `/a` and `path` is `/a/b`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+### Requirement: copy operation
+`copy` SHALL add at `path`, as `add` would, a copy of the value at `from`, which MUST exist. Later changes to one location SHALL NOT affect the other.
+
+#### Scenario: Copy is independent
+- **WHEN** `copy` from `/a` to `/b` is followed by `add` at `/b/x` on `{"a":{}}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"a":{},"b":{"x":...}}` with `/a` still `{}`
+
+### Requirement: test operation
+`test` SHALL succeed, leaving the document unchanged, only if the value at `path` (which MUST exist) is equal to `value`, otherwise it SHALL throw an error. Equality: same type; strings and numbers by value; arrays by equal length and element-wise equality in order; objects by the same set of member names with equal values, regardless of member order; `null`, `true`, `false` by identity.
+
+#### Scenario: Equal objects in different order
+- **WHEN** testing `{"a":1,"b":2}` against value `{"b":2,"a":1}`
+- **THEN** the test succeeds
+
+#### Scenario: Type mismatch
+- **WHEN** testing the number `1` against the string `"1"`, or `null` against a missing member
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
